{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1068503-various-physically-oriented-devotions","id":1068503,"title":"Various Physically Oriented Devotions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-26T18:34:20-07:00","id":1068503,"title":"Various Physically Oriented Devotions","content":"<span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">This rather outgrew itself, so I'll leave it here for personal reference but since I have all this written down in multiple other places I might as well just shorten this to the names for easy cross-reference for a friend. Anything with an X was either revoked/removed or not approved.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><i><b>Carnal Reflex (Protean 2 Aspect)</b></i><br /> While aspect is active, add Protean to Initiative. Like a feral animal you take in your enemies, as their bodies telegraph their intentions with predator instincts.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Hunter's Wit (Protean 2 Aspect)</b></i><br /> While aspect is active, ignore penalties to defense from multiple attacks in a round. You can make the most of your position, like an experienced predator among a pack of dogs.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Predator Sight (Protean 4 Aspect)</i></b><br /> Just as Extra Sense gives 1 way of seeing around you, this is effectively all the sensory organs you can muster within yourself.<br /> While this is active, perception rolls are treated as rote.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Abominable Limbs (Protean 4 Aspect)</i></b><br /> Like many insects, you may now have many limbs and alter their proportions to match.<br /> Using this you can benefit from having 4 extra limbs: arms, legs, or tails arranged as you wish.<br /> For every 2 extra arms applied to the same action, +3 Strength. If at least 2 unoccupied, +3 Defense. (Based on Demon's Extra Mech. Limbs)<br /> <br /> <i><b>Feral Intuition (Protean 2, Celerity 2)</b></i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Embody the Beast (Protean 2 or 4, Resilience 2)</b></i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Enduring Knack (Resilience 4, Celerity 2)</b></i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Skin of the Lion (Forced March, Resilience 2)</b></i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Survival Instinct (Resilience 2, Protean 2)</b></i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Iron Fist (Resilience 2, Vigor 2)</b></i> X<br /> <br /> <i><b>Kindred Forge (Protean 2 or 4, Vigor 2, Resilience 1+)</b></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><i><b>Lick the Wounds (Resilience 3, Protean 2)</b></i><br /> <br /> <b><i>Stake the Vice (Vigor 2, Resilience 2, Animalism 4, OR Reason's Salon, Vigor 2)</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Treacherous Whispers</i></b><b><i> (Animalism 1 or more, Obfuscate 3)</i></b><br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ _______________________________________________<br /> <br /> <b><i>Flight Response (Resilience 4, Vigor 3, or Body of Will &amp; Will to Endure)</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Draping the Night (Obfuscate 4, Vigor 3)</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Reliquary of Fangs (Animalism 3, Vigor 3, Beasts of Blood)</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Dead Facsimile (Animalism 2, Obfuscate 4)</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Partial Merge (Protean 1, Vigor 2, Resilience 2)</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Entombed Command (Animalism 3, Vigor 1)</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Feral Penance (Animalism 2, Protean 1)</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Thicken Hide (Animalism 3, Resilience 1)</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Feral Missive (Animalism 5, Vigor 2)</i></b><br /> <br /> <i><b>Militant Passion</b></i><b><i> (Vigor 3, Celerity 3, Resilience 3)</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Eureka Soak (Holdout, Vigor 2, Resilience 3)</i></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><b><i>Bury (Holdout, Vigor 1)</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Remote Protean (Protean 5, Auspex 4)</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Protean Dirge (Protean 2 or 4, Vigor 2)</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>A Proper Burial (Vigor 1, Holdout, Bury)</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Protean Obeisance (Protean 3, Animalism 3)</i></b><br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ _______________________________________________<br /> <br /> <b><i>Serve With Your Life (Animalism 2, Protean 3, Resilience 1)</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Putty (Protean 1, Vigor 1, Resilience 1)</i></b> X<br /> <br /> <b><i>Vessel Prowess (Animalism 2, Protean 3, Beasts of Blood)</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Familiar Swarm (Protean Obeisance, Swarm Form)</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Uncontested Master (Animalism 5, Obfuscate 5, Resilience 5)</i></b> X<br /> <br /> <b><i>True Nature (Force of Nature; Protean 5, Resilience 5, Vigor 5)</i></b> X<br /> <br /> <b><i>Terracotta Bestiary (Protean 3, Animalism 3, Resilience 3)</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Cephalopod Aspiration (Protean 4, Vigor 1+, Resilience 1+)</i></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i>Berserker Draught</i></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i>Vicious Draught</i></b></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 07-10-2017, 07:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T13:25:38-07:00","id":1068831,"title":"","content":"<b>Zen Shot</b> and <b>Vision of the Predator</b> should require Auspex, not Celerity, since they deal with the senses.<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Fist</b> isn't doing anything interesting with that roll, so drop it.<br /> <br /> <b>Lick The Wound</b> and <b>Survival Instinct</b> are pretty bad - Survival Instinct gives you a <i>chance</i> to avoid something that you really shouldn't be worrying about too much once you've gotten enough dots in Resilience. And Lick The Wound... wuh? Where's the Regeneration Devotion?<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> As a side note, your formatting is <i>atrocious</i> - I'm finding it hard to parse out what's <i>actually</i> mechanically relevant, and what's just the description. The &quot;standard&quot; format looks more like these:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions?p=26592#post26592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two ideas that has been on my mind:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Forced March (Celerity 2, Resilience 2)</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2 Vitae</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Scene (One hour)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">This devotion serves as a popular means of overland transportation for Kindred who have learned to toughen their bodies to withstand the dizzying power of Celerity enough to aid their movement for hours on end. The vampire can reflexively spend Vitae to increase her running speed, multiplying her speed by [Celerity + 1] for one hour. While this version of Celerity is invoked, the Kindred cannot use any of Celerity's other active functions without disabling the Forced March, requiring it to be reactivated.<br /> <i>This Devotion Costs 2 Experiences to Learn</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Vaulting (Vigor 2)</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 1 Vitae</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Turn</span></span><br /> <br /> This easily formulated Devotion allows the Kindred to spend 1 Vitae reflexively to multiply the amount of feet jumped by a Successful Strength + Athletics roll by her Vigor dots plus two. This allows the Vampire to jump even greater distances than the enhanced strength of Vigor typically allows. Obviously this power might be a Masquerade breach for anyone who witnesses the unnatural capability of the Kindred.<br /> <br /> <b>Example:</b> <i>Diana is a Daeva who wants to make a vertical standing jump up on top of a semitruck, which is 12 feet tall. She rolls 4 successes on her Strength + Athletics + Vigor roll, allowing her to jump 4 feet up in the air. She spends 1 Vitae reflexively to activate Vaulting, which given her Vigor of 3, increases her jump height from 4 feet to 20 feet in the air. She deftly lands on top of the truck.</i><br /> <i>This Devotion Costs 1 Experience to Learn</i></span><br /> <br /> In a running jump, the current version of Vaulting would let a Size 5 Kindred with 4 successes cross a distance of 105 feet with Vigor 3. Pretty freaky.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope you can see the difference in legibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T13:29:47-07:00","id":1068835,"title":"","content":"It just puts stuff on it's own line, but alright. And the two requiring Auspex were specifically designed with the intent to use Protean instead, mimicking effects of other devotions in crude (even masquerade breaking) ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T13:51:06-07:00","id":1068857,"title":"","content":"My reply above didn't appear after editing my first post / refreshing, my bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":".  Accidental double post. 03-27-2017, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":